IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lrmp-dates`
IMPORT `lrmp-claims`

-- Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1941 (WA) -- worked cases for the questions of a claimant.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts used below`

`DEF` MEANS `defamation`
`SED` MEANS `seduction`
`ENT` MEANS `inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other`
`BPM` MEANS `breach of promise to marry`
`OTHER` MEANS `any other cause of action (for example personal injury or a dust disease)`

`EARN CAP` MEANS `loss or impairment of capacity to earn`
`EARNINGS` MEANS `loss or diminution of future probable earnings`
`EXPENSES` MEANS `a liability to incur expenditure in the future`
`OTHER LOSS` MEANS `another kind of future loss`

`24 Oct 1942` MEANS `the calendar date` 24 10 1942
`25 Oct 1942` MEANS `the calendar date` 25 10 1942
`14 Nov 2005` MEANS `the calendar date` 14 11 2005
`15 Nov 2005` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 11 2005
`21 Mar 2002` MEANS `the calendar date` 21 3 2002
`22 Mar 2002` MEANS `the calendar date` 22 3 2002
`1 Dec 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 12 2024
`2 Dec 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 12 2024
`1 Jun 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2020
`10 Jan 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 1 2026
`3 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 3 3 2026

§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `22 Mar 2002` `falls after` `21 Mar 2002`
#ASSERT NOT (`21 Mar 2002` `falls after` `21 Mar 2002`)

§ `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate`

-- An injury claim accrued 1 Jun 2020, death 3 Mar 2026, in time: survives.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Breach of promise to marry survives too (only its damages are limited, s 4(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `BPM` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The proviso: defamation, seduction, enticement do not survive (the text's no).
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `DEF` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `SED` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `ENT` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Out of time under the Limitation Act 2005: the deposited Act does not answer (fork F1).
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The proviso is answered before the limitation point: defamation out of time is still the text's no.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `DEF` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The 2005 savings edge: accrued 14 Nov 2005, the old s 4 applies (not deposited): NOTHING; accrued 15 Nov 2005: survives.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `14 Nov 2005` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `15 Nov 2005` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The savings point comes before the proviso: defamation accrued 14 Nov 2005 is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `14 Nov 2005` `DEF` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The commencement edge: a death on 24 Oct 1942 is not "after the commencement": NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `24 Oct 1942` `15 Nov 2005` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A death on 25 Oct 1942 passes the commencement gate (the accrual date is artificial, to isolate the gate).
#ASSERT `s 4(1) -- does the claim survive for the estate` `25 Oct 1942` `15 Nov 2005` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 4(1), (4) -- claims against the estate of a person who died`

#ASSERT `s 4(1), (4) -- can I claim against the estate of the person who died` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1), (4) -- can I claim against the estate of the person who died` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `DEF` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1), (4) -- can I claim against the estate of the person who died` `3 Mar 2026` `14 Nov 2005` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1), (4) -- can I claim against the estate of the person who died` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A driver dies in the crash that injures me on 10 Jan 2026: s 4(4) deems the claim to have existed; it survives.
#ASSERT `s 4(4) -- is a claim deemed to have existed against the person before they died` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1), (4) -- can I claim against the estate of the person who died` `10 Jan 2026` `10 Jan 2026` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- They died after the damage: s 4(4) is not needed (the "where" fails, the text's no to this narrow question).
#ASSERT `s 4(4) -- is a claim deemed to have existed against the person before they died` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No claim would have existed even had they lived.
#ASSERT `s 4(4) -- is a claim deemed to have existed against the person before they died` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 4(2)(d), (2a), (3) -- pain and suffering, and the dust-disease exceptions`

-- Arguments: death, accrual, kind, out of time, latent-injury death, asbestos, silica, proceedings instituted and pending.
-- Mesothelioma from asbestos, death 3 Mar 2026, proceedings pending at death: the bar does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same, but no proceedings had been started before death: the bar applies.
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The asbestos date edge: death on 21 Mar 2002 is not "after the day": the bar applies; 22 Mar 2002: it does not.
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `21 Mar 2002` `15 Nov 2005` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `22 Mar 2002` `15 Nov 2005` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Silicosis, death 1 Dec 2024 (not after the day Part 3 commenced): the bar applies; death 2 Dec 2024: it does not.
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `1 Dec 2024` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `2 Dec 2024` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An asbestos death on 1 Dec 2024 still meets s 4(2a) (after 21 Mar 2002): the bar does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `1 Dec 2024` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a latent injury (a fall from scaffolding), proceedings pending: the bar applies.
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A latent injury from neither asbestos nor silica (for example coal dust): the bar applies.
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The claim does not survive (defamation), or is outside the deposited text: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `DEF` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(d) -- does the law stop the estate recovering damages for pain and suffering` `3 Mar 2026` `14 Nov 2005` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 4(2)(a), (e) -- exemplary damages and the lost years`

#ASSERT `s 4(2)(a) -- does the law stop the estate recovering exemplary damages` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(a) -- does the law stop the estate recovering exemplary damages` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `SED` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(e) -- does the law stop the estate recovering earnings for the lost years` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(e) -- does the law stop the estate recovering earnings for the lost years` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 4(2)(b) -- breach of promise to marry`

#ASSERT `s 4(2)(b) -- is the estate's claim for breach of promise to marry limited to damage to the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `BPM` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(b) -- is the estate's claim for breach of promise to marry limited to damage to the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(b) -- is the estate's claim for breach of promise to marry limited to damage to the estate` `3 Mar 2026` `14 Nov 2005` `BPM` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 4(2)(c) -- death caused by the wrong; funeral expenses`

#ASSERT `s 4(2)(c) -- are gains and losses from the death left out of the estate's damages` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(c) -- are gains and losses from the death left out of the estate's damages` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(c) -- are gains and losses from the death left out of the estate's damages` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `ENT` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(c) -- can the estate's damages include funeral expenses` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(c) -- can the estate's damages include funeral expenses` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(2)(c) -- can the estate's damages include funeral expenses` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 4(5) -- dependants`

#ASSERT `s 4(5) -- does the estate's claim cut down the dependants' claim` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `OTHER` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(5) -- does the estate's claim cut down the dependants' claim` `3 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2020` `DEF` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 5 -- discount rate`

-- Arguments: injury, disease, impairment, death, lump sum, kind of loss (then Order in force, rate fixed).
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- does s 5 fix the discount rate for this part of my award` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `EARN CAP` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- does s 5 fix the discount rate for this part of my award` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `EXPENSES` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- does s 5 fix the discount rate for this part of my award` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `EARNINGS` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- does s 5 fix the discount rate for this part of my award` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `EARNINGS` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a lump sum (periodic payments): the "where" fails, the text's no.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- does s 5 fix the discount rate for this part of my award` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `EARN CAP` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another kind of future loss: no.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- does s 5 fix the discount rate for this part of my award` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `OTHER LOSS` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not about personal injury or death (say, property damage): no.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- does s 5 fix the discount rate for this part of my award` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `EXPENSES` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No Order: 6%. An Order of 3%: 3%. Not reached: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- what discount rate applies to my future loss` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `EARN CAP` FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- what discount rate applies to my future loss` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `EARN CAP` FALSE 3 EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- what discount rate applies to my future loss` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `EXPENSES` TRUE 3 EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- what discount rate applies to my future loss` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `EXPENSES` FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(1) -- what discount rate applies to my future loss` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `OTHER LOSS` TRUE 3 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 2, s 3 -- spouses`

#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is my legal personality separate from my spouse's` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is my legal personality separate from my spouse's` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) -- does being married take away any of my legal capacity` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) -- does being married take away any of my legal capacity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
